        <p>DESIRABLE DWELLING-HOUSES AND COTTAGE PROPERTIES, AND LAND FOR WORKS AND BUSINESS PREMISES AT WARRINGTON. TO BE SOLD BY AUCTION pursuant to an Order of the Court of Chancery of the County Palatine of Lam:mbar made in an Action of LILLIS v. COOPER by MR. THOMAS ARTHUR BUTTON, of the Arm of THOMAS SUTTON AND SONS before the Registrar at the PATTER ARMS HOTEL, WARRING- TON, on Wednesday, the 15th February, 1311, at 3 p.m. precisely in the following or such other Lots an may be determined upon at the Auction. Lou I.—A DESIRABLE well-built Dwelling-house situate and being No. 70, Bewmy-street, Warrinetno, now in the occupation of the Rev. F. C. Shinnliffe as tenant thereof at the yearly rent of £26. The house contains two entertaining rooms, live bedrooms, box room, bath room. so., kitchen, scullery sad cellar with yard and out-office,, The tenure is lemehold for a term of 959 years from 1853 at an annual ground rent of .53. Total area of! lend 241 and 6.9ths aware yards or thereabouts. Lor 2.—A DESIKARLE and well built Dwelling- ' bows situate and being No. 72, Bewseywtreet, . Warrington, now in the occupation of Mr. William 1118110 at. tenant thereof at the yearly rent of £26. lie ' botont contains aimilar accommodation to Lot I. . .</p>
