        <p>Lov3.—X COTTAGES, Attune and being Nos. 13 to 23 odd outliners with the land behold the sarne In Olitermtreet. War:Breton, in the respective occupation, of Mr. Blanton end others es weekly tenants. 'I he tenon, is Imachold torn term of 2,000 years from 1780 at an 101.1k1 ironed rent, of E: 12e. 6d. Gross snood rentals £55 IS.. Total aro, if land in this Lot, iticheling site. of cottages, 1018 and 2 9ths quire yards or thereabouts. LoT 3.—sEVEN LI(.IBII,,HOLD COTTA6F.S situate and being Nos, 25 and 31 to 41 odd number. inclusive in Oliver.street, W. rri ngton, in the respeoti ve occupations of Mr. Holmes and other. a. weekly tenants (gross annual rentals £66 14s. Bd.) together with the Fustian Cntting shop now vacant. (formerly two tenements Nov. 27 and 29) in Oliver.street, with the land behind the some. The tenure iv leeeehold torn term of 2,000 yearn from 1780 at an annual ground rent of £3 6s, 9d. Total area nf land in this lot including niten of buildings 1389 ' and 2/9ths squareayards or thereabouts. In lots 3 and 4 se above nppears there is a consider. able area of meant lend subject to very low ground rents. The Leases contain no restriction as to user of the land which is very suitable and capable of easy adaptation for works and brethren premise.. LOT S.—SIX LEASEHOLD COI-rm.:ES situate and being Nos.l, 3,5, 7, and 9 Shepherds-row and No. 10 Orford.etreet, Warrington, aforesaid with the vacant land adjoining the name, together with the wooden erection. used as stables in the respective occupations of Mr. Connor and others as weekly tenants thereof. Gross annual rental £.72 16s. The tenure is leasehold for two several terms of 2,000 from 1773 and 1775 respectively et the respective nnnual ground rents of £2 8.. sd. and Li Os. Ild. Total area of lend Including the site. of the cottages nod buildings 1583 and 2/oth' sqnare yards or thereabouts. In this Loll. apnears there is a considerable quantity of vacant land. The leans contains no restriction on the use of the land for works or business premises and thie sale offers a good opportnnity of acquiring land for such purpose. in the centre of Warrington at a very moderate ground rent. PARTICULARS AND CONDITIONS OF SALE may be had at the Chancery Office, 9, Cook-street. Liverpool ; of the Anotioneers, (Thomaa Sutton end Sons) Leigh-etreet, Werrington, Mr. Albert Warburton, A.R.1.13.A., Bold-street, Warrington ; Messrs. Arthur S. Mather &amp; Son, Solicitors, 13, Harrington-atreet, Liverpool ; Messrs. North, Kirk &amp; Co., Solicitors, 15, Lord-street, Liverpool, and of ROBERT DAVIES rk CO.. Solicitors, Market Pla..w, Warrington.</p>
