        <head>FIT TO WORK Interesting Case at the County Court.</head>
        <p>FIT TO WORK Interesting Case at the County Court.</p>
        <p>At the Warrington Caunty Court, on Thursday, before His Honour, Judge Stenger, K.C., Mr. A. Browne, on behalf of Mesa.. Bylands, Limited, applied for the review of an order made in the Court under the Work- tuen's Compensation Act by seaward for Harry Trigger a joiner, against Messrs. Ityltinday, whereby the latter bed to pay Lie week during the time that Trigger wi - incapacitated. Mr. St. al appeared for Trigger. Mr. Graham Mil. Benton, senior house saw on at the Itroyni Infirmary, Manche ter, stated that he remembered the man lining admitted to the Infirmary on December 2181. Vit.. examined the man hut ' could riot tlid anything the matter with him. Triggr took his dischnrce the following morning. Witnesn agreed with Dr. Richmond that Trigger wee r •rt, Illy fit to rerun. work raft joiner. hi r. Walter Barker, cashier ta Messrs. Ryland, Her- niated that he had paid Trigger El a week once the tittle of the accident. Trigger told him on January 6111 that be wen reedy to came back to work. Mr. Steel : Anil were you willing to II id him work ?—That is nut for me to say. It is not in my apartment. NIL Steel, for the respondent, /laid he did not think it was a case in which there ought to boa termination of the agreement Bled in that court. When the evid- ence of Trigger had been heard it would be 119.3 that he could not obtain employment with any other works in Warrington. Trigger wean called, and slated in annwer to Mr. Steel that when he .ine from the klanchetner Infltruary he saw Mr. Barker, nod he inked witness when be thought he would be able to start work. Witnern told him he would try to work then. He went to Mr. Howarth, the manager at Rylands, and asked brim for work, but he said he had no lacancy. Rots day later Mr. Howarth took another elan on. Witness had tried at several works for employment hut they would not start him. Mr. Steel : Do you think yau would bo nafe going up n ladder, or standing nod working on a roof.—Nu,</p>
        <p>Ills Honour made the order for a termination of the agreement with costs on scale ft remarking that et the tame time ho boyad Messrs. Itylands would take Trigger on at the earliest opportunity.</p>
