        <p>Interesting Debate. The most interesting di‘euesion Id the monthly meet- . g of the Warrington 'f own Connuil on Tneeday oven• g was occasioned by the reconiMeiniation of the '•enoral Plirposes Comm i it.. That the wilary of he Town Clerk ho increased by the num of £2Ol per 5.11 m."</p>
        <p>...... 'IhoMIV4,II. MoVIA and the 1.41'1,Y MA VOll imcomini the confirmation of the General Purpriemi Commit 'en minntea. . .</p>
        <p>..... ..... (Joticrel (or A,11,1[017 moved that the minute relat- ing to the propneed increams iif the Town Chirk'snalliry be referred hack. The loot? ion wan enddenly nJrllng upon the committee by Aldermen Pinpoint without any notice—in fact It waa like ?Ailing ri lents in the dark, lie considered that nneh an important mat ter drool,! 'nave been more folly di.mined after duo notice. . .</p>
