        <p>The following year his successes included :—Firot at Balliol-road, Liverpool ; first at Altrineham ; and second to T. Pemberton in the Warrington champion- ship. In 1905 he won the championship M I min. t9:l.stwes. The following year he was again Necond o his rival T. Pemberton in the championship and second in the 151 yards rare at Rock Savag, In lag he wan first in the 50 yards !handicap at Ramsey, 1.0. M. Ile alio achieved the brilliant performance of carrying oil he Warrington Championship in the record lime of 1 min. 50secs. lie again secured the championship in 1900 in Imin. 51sees., and ia 1999 in imin. :,3.ecn. That year he was firvt in dm DO yard. and 2'l yards aandicape at Douglas, 1.0 M., and first at Widec. In 1910 he won the kcal championship for the :Ali time in twin. 51secs., and was again first at Widnes. At the opening of Stockton Heath lake Mr. Allen gave all exhibition of swimming, on which be was highly complimented. Mr. Allen in also a runner or some repute and in 1903 he won the seven miles novice race in connection with Sankey Harrier..</p>
        <p>In his new sphere Mr. Allen will carry with him the good wishes f a numerous circle of friends. Tha employees of the Firth Co., where he has been empb.yed for 60111 e yearn, hive shown their regard by presenting him with a dressing case.</p>
