        <head>ARPLEY FIELDS ASSAULT.</head>
        <p>THE ARPLEY FIELDS ASSAULT.</p>
        <p>HARRIS CONFESSES TO FURTHER OFFENCES. An echo of the Arpley fields &amp;smolt case, wan breed St the Borough Police Court on Monday morning, ',heats charge of stealing £4 16a from anhop in Orford- Inns. wan preferred against Herrin (who is now serving a term of imprisonment) and another youth named Stokes. Stokes wan before the Court a week apo on the charge and was then remanded in order that Harris, might he brought from prison. It was stated by the chief-conarahle on that occasion that while Herds was in prison he bad written a state- ment confessing ta 6,Pral theftn,and vaying he desired to clear his character and make n fresh start when he come out of prison. In this statement he implicated Stokes.—On klondes it was stated by the chief- conntahle Mut on November 160909, Mr.. Ground!,</p>
        <p>. the owner of a grocer's , hop, 54, Orfo rd- la ne, had ter...ion to go out of town, leaving over £4 in the till. lie did not return until late at night when he found his shop broken open Rild the money gone from the till. The polio. were not informed at the time, and conse- quently no enquirits veto made. The next that was heard of the theft ens when a letter ass received trvm the Governor of klanchester prison stating that Harris had made a statement confessing to the thef,. As far as Barris on, concerned, the Chief Consrahle added, he would like him to he sent to the Quarter Sessionn where ho could he put under the Borstal its. rem. ila ens doing a great amount of harm to other lads in the town.</p>
        <p>Thin coarse WWI agreed to, the Chairmen remarking, " Perrin, yeit have the makings of a criminal in you. and you certainly require some very special treatment." In the case fir Stokes, the Chief Coenobite said that he thought they could diechnrge him, after binding him over for 12 Imitator in hie own recognineneee, hie Grntber.in-law having promised to look after him. Stokes expreetred himself as very sorry, and the course was adopted.</p>
