      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-02-11_WidnesExaminer_art0091" n="art0091">
        <head>MEDICAL SUMMONS.</head>
        <p>A MEDICAL SUMMONS.</p>
        <p>STRANGE PI.OSECUTION AT BOROUGH COURT.</p>
        <p>An Interesting case came before the Werringtnn Borough Bench on Tuesday, (Councillor Henry Roberts presiding, o hen Annie Smallrnan, 12. Iloweridatreet, men summoned hy the Warrineton Education Corn. mites with neglecting her child, Thomas Smallmen, aged 10,10 P manner likely to cause him uonecee•ary suffering and injury to health. It was stated hy Mr. A.T. liallswey (deputy Town Clerk that proceeding, had been laid under section 1.1 of the Children.' Act of 1900. Tbe section mates that "ifs person over the riga of In years who has the, custody, charge, or care of any child or young person nilfolly assault., ill-trents or neglects such child inn manner likely to cause unnecesaery stiffering or injury to keulth,that wenn shell he Reilly of a misdemeanour' The section Mr. Hallaway said, went on to say that if the custodiao of a child failn to provide eufficient medical aid that will also be considered . rnis- demesne., In this particular case the boy had been examined by the school medical officer in accordance with the provicionn of the Administration Education Act (1907). HP was found lobe suffering from !adenoids. Dr. Hutt would be called and would tell the Bench that adenoids would cause the gravest nuffering to thie chi Id. The mother wee informed in July teat, and told that the child would have to be treated. Sp far the child bad not seen the doctor. Mrs. Sinallman wes three time, before the Medical Inepeclon Committee, end the In•pector called at her house at least 12 times urging her to bane the child attended to. The mother was before the Comm itsves in September of lent year, when it was ascertained that the child had been run over by a motor one, and at that time the mother said she did not think the child wee Otto be treated. She tees told In bring the chill to the doctor to ace if he We. St to be treated, butthe child wee never brought. Thedoctor however, examined the child last 31tindar, and he found that be was quite ready for trentrnent. Ily prosecitting in these CIIECS Mr.Hallaway ecided,it brought the per•llls ton sense of their responsibility. Dr. Hutt (aeeistant medical officer of health), stated that he examined the child on 30th January, and found it suffering front adenoids. He coneidersd that if the boy was not treated harm would accrue. Defendant stated that tin reason she did not allow the boy to be treated can been». she Old not think he Ives in a fit state after hie ecoident to undergo the treatment.</p>
        <p>The cane sena adjourned torn month, the child in the meantime to go coder treatment.</p>
