        <head>Borough Police Court.</head>
        <p>Borough Police Court.</p>
        <p>MONDA V.—Before the Mayor (in the chair), Aldermen Pierpoint, Smethuret, Bolton, and lames Evans. Cutincillors IL Roberts and J. W. Wilkionon, and . S. Wright, J. W. Has ward, W. Roberts. T. Locker, H. Thornton and G. Pilling. A DOMESTIC SERVANT'S TIILET.—N.IiiAbeth Walton was remanded for seven days on a charge of stealing from a Louse. 46, Banter-street, Se. in casb.—lt was stated ho tie Chief Constable that the girl went to the house and said she !mew a Mr. Martin, at Su:Mulch, a gt °Unman whom the prnsecut or knew. He took her in and gene her some food, hut when she had gone he missed the money. It was added that it Wee 'Dry likely Oat another cnse of • similar nature would lop preferred against prisoner. DEbERTED III• %VIER AND Clitsnitsx.—John Magma, Evelyn•ntreet, who wan charged with denertiog his wife cad children, leaning them chargeable to the Warring. 'on Union, was bound :over in his owe recognisances, for three months.—Mr. Sharer etated that prisoner went away whilst out of employment, bet Pince he had returned he had obtained work. It was not ovary bed case, he added.—The Chairman Hos be gone back to his wife.—Mr. Shearer Yes. sir ;he i• living with her now. THCRBDAV.—Refore . John Fairclongh (in the cheir), W. Roberts, Edwin Woods, A. J. Jolley, W. T. Williams, 1. l'peon, IV. hones., T. Locker, IV. Richardson, R. T. Fairclough, and Dr. Naden. A FATHER'', NEOLE. T.—The Isle of a father's neglect was related when John Lindley, of 2, Dial. court, wee charged with sbandoning his two children. and Also with neglecting them in a metier likely to cause them unnecesnarx suffering and injsry to health.—lt was stated by Mr. A. Browne, who appeared for the N.S.P.C.C., that defendant left home on Satur- day and did not return. Newtons to tint whilst earn- ins 21s. • week he had only given his wife small sums. —lnspector Wainwright of the N.S.I'.C.C. mated that he had visited the house and had had to supply coal,food and light. Ou Saterday the wife bed to get assistance from the Union.—The Cl.lairman, in adjourning the case for teo monthu maid he hoped it would be a warning to defendant. WEDNRSDAT.—Before Meagre. Charles White 'in the chair), J. W. Hayward, and Councillor Jackson- Holmes. THEFT or En os.—A amatl flee nf 511. and costs wile imposed on a renpectable-dressed middle-aged men named John Ashley,Thelwall•lane,who was charged with the theft of four eggs.—lt was stated that prisoner wry seen on Tuesday morning near a shop in Market-street and take the eggs. Tee police were informed and he was arrested, The Chairman Was he intoxicated nt the tinie ?—The Chief Constable : Slightly, sir, and that was at ten o'clock In the morning. bolt, \ V.—Before the Mayor On the chair) and other magistratee. A BOTTLE WHISKY AND RESlTT.—ElizAbeth Latin, a married woman, residing at Portland-street, Warrington, presented a pitiful appearance when placed in the dock on • cherge of stealing a bvttle of whisky from the King's Arms Hotel, Iltittermarket-street, on Thursday.—The Chief Cunstable nutted that the woman went into the her about 1.30 p.m. and ordered a glans of beer. %Odle there it was noticed that she behaved in enspiciodll meaner and when she bad left, a bottle of whinky was found to be mining. Later prisoner was seen to visit several times no outhouse near her house, nach time tubing a nip of the spirits. She was arreeted and brought to the police station, added the Chief Constable, in a helple-s state of alcoholism.—ln reply to all questions prisoner replied, "I cannot remember." —She nes bound over to keep the peace for twelve months. ALI.E..ED Tug, Moll A LODGING HOCSE.— Edward Senmel, n lodging•house habitue, WAS remanded • until Tuesday on a cherge of stealing On. from a fellow lodger. It was atated that prisoner was seen to turn all the lights down in the room and then take the</p>
