      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-02-11_WidnesExaminer_art0098" n="art0098">
        <head>St. Paul's CN S.</head>
        <p>St. Paul's CN S.</p>
        <p>The yeses work in connection with St. Paul's branch of the Church Missionary Society has been entirely succesful. as was evidence] by the treasurer's report at the first annual meeting held in the Kendrick-street Infent sohools held on Wednesday evening. The Rev. E. E. Petere presided over a good attendance. The treasurer Mr. A. C. fiche) stated that the amount raised during the year wee .£lO Is. 7d. During the evening, the Rev. A. J. (Welch, the now diriceittn secretary of the society,delivered an interesting ad tried; on Locknow. India, lantein illustrations adding to the success of the lecture.</p>
