        <p>Two or three billion germs could be excreted from one person alone in a day. "'be building st Sankey wm lying idle. It cost £9,060, end was intended for the ,1 ore of smell-pox patients, but, in his opinion, small pox was dead letterin IVarriugton practically. the town we. so well vaccinated and they had not a 'owl chance of having, if they wanted one, a vim small-pi, epidemic. , Laughter and boar, heard This place shonlil he need for the beneti. of the community in the way proposed. Councillor BIRTI.E9 asked if it were the intention of the committee to close the houses in Ilughes-court and Cambria-place, whore he noticed closing orders had been made. If they were to be closed he would like to know whether there want, bis made mey provi- sion for the tenants. To those people who had been in the houses for 30 or 40 yearn it wag a great hariship, unless the Council were in • position to provide place. for the unhoused tenants abo could not afford to yar much rent. lie had seen the houses and found them almost tumbling down far want of repair. They , belonged to the Corporation and the owners were largely to blame for their had suite. la some cases they had not been painted for twelve years. The Cor- poration could not expect them to lie in a sanitnry condition when they lied been allowed to go to rack and ruin. They ought to erect dwellings to meet such cases or give every consideration to tenants in the hours..</p>
        <p>Ilambitotts said that the mere fact tint there was no opposition to the proposal regsrding phthisis ItbOWBCI that the Council w. with them. nom the estimate of the Medical °dicer, the ctst of utillz- ing the building would</p>
