      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-02-11_WidnesExaminer_art0119" n="art0119">
        <head>FIRST STATE OPENING OF PARLIAMENT IN THE NEW REGN.</head>
        <p>THE FIRST STATE OPENING OF PARLIAMENT IN THE NEW REGN.</p>
        <p>King George, accompanied by Queen Mary, opened, this week, the first-elected Parliament of his reign, with the dignity and splendour with which the ages have clothed the ceremony. Their Majesties' journey from Buckingham Palace to Westminster was witnessed by tremendous crowds, who demonstrated their loyally by hearty cheering, and, almost for the first time since tbe death of King Edward, London seemed to awake to a realization of the pageantry of Sovereignty and State. Oar picture skews Use State Coach, drawn by the famous creams, passing along Whltchall.</p>
        <p>A glimpse of Their Majesties the King and Queen, in the gorgeous Coach of State, drawn by the eight famous cream ponies with their purple and gilt trappings. On each side marched Yeomen of the Guard in their full dress of scarlet and gold, and carrying their halberds on their shoulders.</p>
