      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-02-11_WidnesExaminer_art0141" n="art0141">
        <head>HOCKEY.</head>
        <p>HOCKEY.</p>
        <p>Latchford had silos gams with Manchester University at Fallowileld last Saturday, and made n draw of 0-0. The University now have a first-close ground which favours faat hockey. TN, first half was in favour of Latchford. Their forwards got in sorne neat paroling at this period of the game and I. perlenced hard lines when Parker struck the upright with a clinking shot, which had the Mancheeter keeper well beaten. The / second half favoured Miinchmter, and the visiting half backr had sil their work out out to keep the l'niversity forwards within bounds. The fall-hack. ale° ;dived .tesdily. The main,festure of the match was the clever I manner in which flill kept goal for Latchford. Shots of all kinds were along at him, but he repelled them with great skill, and undoubtedly Ind much to do with Mancheater not taking the lead. The game was a thoroughly enjoyable one from start to finish.. .</p>
        <p>The "eacond elevens met at Latchford and a close game ended in favour of the home team by 4-3. visiting cents, quickly gave his side the lead after floe router play, but Pearson equalized with .4 high dropping idiot from Ulu right. Following god centres ' from the right wing Starkey then shot two goals and at before half-tint. Banks merle the ems, I• 1 with smart goal. lo the sucond half Mancheiter, we, the beet team and scored twice. The home forwerde Isere rugged after half time land were frequently frustrated by thu visitors right full-back who presented W very 1.11 front end cleared well. For Latchford Weis* did good defeesive work binder pressure. Latchford, were lucky to maintain their lead.</p>
