        <head>u DISTRICT ri Ews ij</head>
        <p>u DISTRICT ri Ews ij</p>
        <p>Moore.</p>
        <p>LAN LECTI.RE.-9n Wedneetiev evening Mr.</p>
        <p>I Kenneth Bishop -of 'Sloe' k-to'n 'Heath gave a lecture on t' A Holiday on Tyneside," to tbe memliore of the Wesley Guild. Mr. J. Jackaon presided over a good attendance. The lecture was ill...tooted with about • handred end thirty magnificent elides. NI, Bishop is so expert photographer sodas might have heen expected the slides were of a very high order indeed and the subjects were so very various and yet every otte equally interesting that the audience were delighted. After the lecture Miss Dutton very ahly expreseed the thanks of the Luild to Mr. Bishop for his lecture, Mr. Lawton seconded and it was carried with applause. Culcheth.</p>
        <p>Sol IA I. AT Zi KW C III" RC IL—A ten party and social promoted by the choir and bellriugers of the New- church Par;sh Conrch woo held in the P.P. schools on Stiturisy evening last. About 50 sat down to tea.after shioh dancing was indulged in. Solos were song by Miss Nladdock and Mr. A. Lawton, the accompanist being Mr. James Orme. Tot 1,, GREEN iNI,RVICNDENT METIIODISTS.—The monthly P.S.A. in connection with this place was held on Suminy afternoon, presided over by 51r. J. Aldred. address was</p>
        <p>A very instructive and interesting given to the teachers and scholars by Mr. lVelsby, of Culobeth. Solos were very ably rendered by the Mi Barton nod Runcorn ; tries by the :Views Runcorn, Bic/erste nod Mr. E. Barton ; 'tat ions by the Misses R. Snob!. and A. Broadhurst. There was a good attendance and the guesting was very enjoyable.</p>
