      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-02-11_WidnesExaminer_art0144" n="art0144">
        <head>Daresbu. j.</head>
        <p>Daresbu. j.</p>
        <p>1100 t, TREAT.—Th,, mooed winter treat to the Sunday school scholars attending the Church Schools at Deresbury. Moore, l'reston Brook, and Hatton took place on the 3rd. inst., when 110 children sat down to tea in the 'Council School. After tea a very large Bomber of beautiful books were distributed as prises to those most regular in attendance and exemplary in conduct. Mrs. Lee-tones distributed the award.. Six children attending the Hatton School, mined Thorne. Houghton, Pe .cy Cliffe, Alice Clifie, Elsie &amp;moister, Clara Wainwright and Stanley &amp;moister, had been proaent every time the school had met. In addition to book prizes they were given it certificate of merit and complimented by the Vicar upon their excellent atten- dance. After the distribution a most enjoyable enter- tainment by means of a Punch and Judy" Show was given. Before separating hearty cheers. proposed by the Vieer,were accorded to the teachers and to Alr. find Wright for their tr.itible in preparing the tee, nod to Mrs. Lee-Jones for distributing the prism.</p>
