        <p>Sir,--It is-prop—id the Mary's of the British I Empire shell viler a gift to Her Majesty the Queen, and at the request of the Secretary for Lancashire (the Dowager Lady Gerard) I have under- taken the collection in the Warrington district. All those who bear the Lame of Mary, Maris, May or Marian are invited to submits, any sum not exceed-, ing £l. Subscriptions (under ccver endorsed may De forwarded to me at the Town Hall, where a list will be kept of all subscriptions received. The Warrington Fund will close on Wednesday the Bth March.—l am.sir. vows &amp;c., PHYLLIS JOSEPH (Mayoress). Town Hall, I,.'arrington. 10th February, 1911.</p>
