        <head>CROSS COUNTRY RUNNING.</head>
        <p>CROSS COUNTRY RUNNING.</p>
        <p>/MINT LANCASIIIRX CHAMPEONSHIP.-11.• West Walshlna province of the Northern Amociation held their initial divisional championships it Rylanda Recreation Ground. Gurney-leer, in splendid weather, before • good master of apectators. The junior race lied attracted entries from 15 team. of whom only Holm* Hullers (Carnforthi wore absentees. Starter Waterloo got the 134 runners awe, on equitable terms sod the field presented • pretty sight as the varied uniforms of the clubs rushed round the enclosure ate very rapid mt., the red and white of Warrington, the green and white of Sacred Heart, and the Royal Blue of Rylands' were early prominent and led the way into the country compriaing momo ploughed land which, owing to the recent frost, provided • severe test and in several oases proved the undoing of some fancied candi- dates. C.. 1. Rryent, Preston Harriers, Ira. always well placed and eventually won comfortably by about fifty yard. io • style suggestive of further success. Results INDIVIDUAL POSITIONS. Mi.. Soy.</p>
