        <p>Teams: Sacred Heart (6,10, 11, 13, (9, 26) 85 points: Warrington AC (4, 11, 15, IS, 25, 29), 109 points ; Runcorn Tally Ho, 151) ; Lancruiter Park, 193 ; Sharron, 240; Richmond, 242 ; Rol:morn Holy Trinity, 286 ; Preaton 11, 298. The Brat four teams and Bryant. Fisharick and Pregson as individual, or unplaced teams ere eligible to compete in the Northern Junior Championehlp proper it Haydoek Perk next Saturday and should , maluteln the reputstion of the province.</p>
        <p>&amp;yea olobs had ente'red ;;I all except Wallasey A.C. competed over a course of shoot eight mike. Confident of their condition the Warrington Inds out • very hot pace and before l miles had been covered the field wee strung out with a tall quite a quarter of a mil* long. H Holbrook nod C Tose were in Pont almost through- out sod the former won by about 70 yards. S Welding sod .1 T Simmer made numerous efforts to overhaul the leaders but without making soy impreseion and the latter bad to go all out to stave off a determined chsllcnce from IV Holton, another local.</p>
        <p>, C.l Straw met with • alight mishap In the early Magee of the race, sod hle withdrawal was • serious matter for Sutton, as it left the local. with • good lead, A Wiloock• and A Siddall of Warrington. wore in prominent positions when they were oompelled to to retire. Thu enconraged, the Sutton men ran deeperatelyAnd • mile from the finish only a few points separated the clubs. W Antrobue, 11 K Jepson. and T Wall ran resolutely in the closing etageq, and Warring- ton won by 10 point• after • dour struggle. Result : INDIVIDUAL POSITIONS. Mink Secs. 1 H Holbrook, Warrington A.C. 2 C VON.. Warrington A.C. 3 8 Welding, Sot ton Harriers 4 Jl' Simmer, Sefton Harriers 47 53 °IS W Holton, Warrington A.C. S. E Harrieon, Sutton 7 8 Franoom, Sefton 8 .1 Smart, Sutton 4B 21 9 L Drinitester, St H•lene Rea H 10 W Antrobus, Warrington AC 4B 29 11 H Hardman, Sutton 49 34 12 H K Jepson, Warrington AC 49 42 13 Wll Begg, Sutton 14 A Maohlaster, West Chadds* H 15 J Morrie, Sutton 16 T Wall, Warrington AC 49 44 17 TF Turtoo, Wm-rington AC 49 54 18 E Anders, Sutton 5O 15 19 SK Hayward, West Cheshire 20_W Barge. WeetCheshire 5O 36 ... . .</p>
        <p>Team. : N'srrington AC (I, 2,5, 10, 12, IR) 46 points ; Sulton flarriers (3, R. 2, 11. IS, 15) 50/ poisls ; West Cheehire Harritp.rs.42l points ; Sefton Harriers 131</p>
        <p>These teams are eligible to compete in the senior championship of the Northern Crow Country Association.</p>
        <p>Liverpool Herders and SL Helens Rece each failed to finish the necessary six men to count a teem. Jorrm,</p>
        <p>Amongst those present were the 31syor (Dr. Joseph), Mr. W. P. itylande and Mr.A. H. Crosfield, the Mayoress (Miss Joseph) and many other ladies also graced the occasion by their presence and apparently enjoyed the sport. Marrs. H Maddock and C BIM) proved themselves efficient clerks of the copse. The •rrangements were satisfsetory to all concerned and as a sporting event the meeting wee • pronounced MICCI,I. Many van witnessed snob MOS for the first tints I expressed their intention of spending a couple of shill- Ingo, shoot all the outing need cost, in a visit to Haydock Park nest Saturday. On Thursday the ntid.week section of Warrington A.C. no oil their first handicap over shoot 11,8 COMM with the following result :—Sidney Grounds, scratch, IC Nurse scratch, .1 Toralioson 1 snin.,T Conroy, 1 min. A good ram throughout. Grounds' superior pace enebled him to win bv three yards front Nurse who beat I Mpg by shout 30 prds with the others close op. Warrington A.O fixture to-dey is from the Royal Oak Branch.</p>
